-- Crimes Regulations 2019 -- worked cases, from the seat of the person with a conviction (REQ-0097). Expected values were
-- written by hand from the deposited Regulations (Compilation No. 5, F2025C01226) and Part VIIC of the Act, never copied from
-- the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL. A Commonwealth offence, conviction 15 March 2016, no prison, not a
-- minor: spent from 15 March 2026 (ca14-cases-accused.l4).

-- Which bodies are prescribed.
#ASSERT `Is the screening body prescribed` `WA: the CEO under the Working with Children (Criminal Record Checking) Act 2004` `work with children`
#ASSERT `Is the screening body prescribed` `WA: the CEO under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Screening) Act 2020` `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the screening body prescribed` `WA: the CEO under the Working with Children (Criminal Record Checking) Act 2004` `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)`
#ASSERT `Is the screening body prescribed` `Vic: the Secretary under the Worker Screening Act 2020` `work with children`
#ASSERT `Is the screening body prescribed` `Vic: the Secretary under the Worker Screening Act 2020` `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)`
#ASSERT `Is the screening body prescribed` `SA: the central assessment unit under the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016` `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)`
#ASSERT `Is the screening body prescribed` `Qld: the Queensland College of Teachers` `work with children`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the screening body prescribed` `ACT: an independent advisor under the Working with Vulnerable People (Background Checking) Act 2011` `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the screening body prescribed` `another person or body, such as an aged care worker screening body` `work with people accessing funded aged care`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the screening body prescribed` `NSW: the Children's Guardian (working with children check)` `work with people accessing funded aged care`

-- A Perth applicant for a WA working with children check, 1 June 2026: the CEO may be told and take it into account.
#ASSERT `Must I disclose this conviction to the screening body` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE `WA: the CEO under the Working with Children (Criminal Record Checking) Act 2004` `work with children` FALSE FALSE 0 (Date 15 3 2016) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes, if asked: although my conviction is spent, Part VIIC Division 6 lets this person or body be told and take it into account for this purpose (ss 85ZZGB-85ZZGD, 85ZZH)`
-- The same person applying for WA NDIS worker screening.
#ASSERT `Must I disclose this conviction to the screening body` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE `WA: the CEO under the National Disability Insurance Scheme (Worker Screening) Act 2020` `work with people with disability (NDIS worker screening)` FALSE FALSE 0 (Date 15 3 2016) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes, if asked: although my conviction is spent, Part VIIC Division 6 lets this person or body be told and take it into account for this purpose (ss 85ZZGB-85ZZGD, 85ZZH)`
-- Aged care worker screening: nobody is prescribed, so the spent conviction is protected.
#ASSERT `Must I disclose this conviction to the screening body` (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE `another person or body, such as an aged care worker screening body` `work with people accessing funded aged care` FALSE FALSE 0 (Date 15 3 2016) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: my conviction is spent, so I need not disclose that I was charged with or convicted of the offence, I may lawfully say I was not, and anyone who knows must not disclose it or take it into account without my consent (ss 85ZV, 85ZW)`
-- Before it was spent (1 June 2020): disclose if asked.
#ASSERT `Must I disclose this conviction to the screening body` (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE `WA: the CEO under the Working with Children (Criminal Record Checking) Act 2004` `work with children` FALSE FALSE 0 (Date 15 3 2016) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes, if asked: my conviction is not spent, so Part VIIC gives me no right not to disclose it`
-- A WA (State) offence before a WA body: the State's law decides.
#ASSERT `Must I disclose this conviction to the screening body` (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `WA: the CEO under the Working with Children (Criminal Record Checking) Act 2004` `work with children` FALSE FALSE 0 (Date 15 3 2016) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `my conviction is for a State offence and the person asking is not a Commonwealth authority in a State: the State's own spent convictions law decides it (s 85ZV(2), (3)), and that law is not encoded here`
